WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:02.734
-Republicans have narrowly
won back

00:00:02.734 --> 00:00:04.934
the House of Representatives,
but they'll have to navigate

00:00:04.934 --> 00:00:07.100
the next two years
with a very small majority,

00:00:07.100 --> 00:00:09.968
which will likely cause chaos
and empower fringe extremists,

00:00:09.968 --> 00:00:11.300
like Marjorie Taylor Greene.

00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:12.801
And all of that
will be happening

00:00:12.801 --> 00:00:14.868
as Donald Trump
tears the party further apart

00:00:14.868 --> 00:00:16.067
with his presidential bid.

00:00:16.067 --> 00:00:18.234
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:18.234 --> 00:00:22.367
♪♪
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:22.367 --> 00:00:24.467
Today was a big day
on Capitol Hill.

00:00:24.467 --> 00:00:26.234
Outgoing House Speaker
Nancy Pelosi,

00:00:26.234 --> 00:00:28.634
who has made history as the
first woman to lead the chamber,

00:00:28.634 --> 00:00:30.400
announced that she would
not seek reelection

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:32.868
to a leadership position
in the next Congress.

00:00:32.868 --> 00:00:35.234
In her speech, she noted
how many presidents

00:00:35.234 --> 00:00:37.033
she has worked with
across party lines,

00:00:37.033 --> 00:00:39.701
although, she left out
one notable name.

00:00:39.701 --> 00:00:42.434
-Been my privilege
to play a part

00:00:42.434 --> 00:00:45.267
in forging
extraordinary progress

00:00:45.267 --> 00:00:46.601
for the American people.

00:00:46.601 --> 00:00:49.767
I have enjoyed working
with three presidents.

00:00:49.767 --> 00:00:53.634
Achieving historic investments
in clean energy

00:00:53.634 --> 00:00:55.901
with President George Bush.

00:00:55.901 --> 00:00:58.067
[ Applause ]

00:00:58.067 --> 00:01:02.000
Transformative healthcare reform
with President Barack Obama.

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:04.033
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:01:04.033 --> 00:01:05.400
And forging --

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:07.567
And forging the future,

00:01:07.567 --> 00:01:09.234
from infrastructure
to healthcare,

00:01:09.234 --> 00:01:12.901
to climate action,
with President Joe Biden.

00:01:12.901 --> 00:01:14.901
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:01:14.901 --> 00:01:16.501
[ Laughter ]
-Say what you will
about Nancy Pelosi,

00:01:16.501 --> 00:01:18.000
but she knows what she's doing.

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:21.100
[ Laughter ]
The worst thing you can do
to Donald Trump

00:01:21.100 --> 00:01:22.601
is not say anything
about Donald Trump.

00:01:22.601 --> 00:01:24.934
[ Laughter ]
The man desperately
craves attention.

00:01:24.934 --> 00:01:26.567
He'd rather you call him
a disgusting,

00:01:26.567 --> 00:01:28.801
degenerate criminal moron
than not say his name.

00:01:28.801 --> 00:01:31.334
And I'm sure he watched
that speech,

00:01:31.334 --> 00:01:33.234
since he's always watching TV.

00:01:33.234 --> 00:01:35.267
[ Laughter ]
Right now he's probably at home,
spinning out, saying --

00:01:35.267 --> 00:01:37.133
[ As Trump ]
Wait a second.
Does Nancy not like me?

00:01:37.133 --> 00:01:38.634
[ Laughter ]

00:01:38.634 --> 00:01:40.067
What did I ever do to her?

00:01:40.067 --> 00:01:42.167
Oh, right.
Oh, yeah.

00:01:42.167 --> 00:01:43.601
[ Laughter ]
Oh, and there was that.

00:01:43.601 --> 00:01:45.367
Oh, ho, ho, that was a bad one.

00:01:45.367 --> 00:01:47.133
[ Laughter ]

00:01:47.133 --> 00:01:49.934
Compare Pelosi's farewell
address to Trump's announcement

00:01:49.934 --> 00:01:52.167
that he's running for president,
for a third time,

00:01:52.167 --> 00:01:53.334
which is full of lies

00:01:53.334 --> 00:01:55.367
and mangled sentences
and weird tangents.

00:01:55.367 --> 00:01:58.133
Trump's speech has also sparked
yet another round

00:01:58.133 --> 00:02:00.901
of infighting and recriminations
among Republicans,

00:02:00.901 --> 00:02:03.534
given that Trump has repeatedly
tanked the party.

00:02:03.534 --> 00:02:05.501
He did in 2018, 2020,

00:02:05.501 --> 00:02:07.868
and then again
in last week's midterms,

00:02:07.868 --> 00:02:09.467
and, yet, Trump,
obviously, does not care.

00:02:09.467 --> 00:02:10.868
On Tuesday,
he announced his intention

00:02:10.868 --> 00:02:13.467
to take back
the corridors of power,

00:02:13.467 --> 00:02:15.601
although, as usual, he tripped
up on the word and then,

00:02:15.601 --> 00:02:18.000
because he was too embarrassed
to correct himself,

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:21.100
repeated it a bunch of times
to try to save face,

00:02:21.100 --> 00:02:22.334
which only made it worse.

00:02:22.334 --> 00:02:24.300
-This is our country,
our government,

00:02:24.300 --> 00:02:26.534
and the carters of power --

00:02:26.534 --> 00:02:28.767
or our --
they're our carters.

00:02:28.767 --> 00:02:29.901
They're not their carters.

00:02:29.901 --> 00:02:32.534
[ Laughter ]
These are our carters.

00:02:32.601 --> 00:02:33.467
[ Laughter ]

00:02:33.467 --> 00:02:35.734
And we are coming

00:02:35.734 --> 00:02:38.300
to take those carters back.

00:02:38.300 --> 00:02:40.501
[ Laughter ]

00:02:40.501 --> 00:02:42.000
-Can I just pitch you something?

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:43.234
Try halls.

00:02:43.234 --> 00:02:44.667
[ Laughter ]

00:02:44.667 --> 00:02:45.934
Halls of power.

00:02:45.934 --> 00:02:46.934
[ Laughter ]

00:02:46.934 --> 00:02:48.167
So, clearly, what happened here

00:02:48.167 --> 00:02:50.300
is he stumbled on the word
corridors once

00:02:50.300 --> 00:02:51.934
and then said it like
eight more times

00:02:51.934 --> 00:02:53.868
[ Laughter ]
to try and recover,
which is not how you do it.

00:02:53.868 --> 00:02:55.901
It's like if you called someone
the wrong name during sex

00:02:55.901 --> 00:02:57.300
and then just kept saying it,

00:02:57.300 --> 00:02:59.934
in hopes that they would choose
to legally chain it.

00:02:59.934 --> 00:03:01.100
[ Laughter ]

00:03:01.100 --> 00:03:02.634
Lisa -- I mean,
you're not a Lisa,

00:03:02.634 --> 00:03:03.701
but you look like a Lisa.

00:03:03.701 --> 00:03:04.734
[ Laughter ]
And Lisa, what a name --

00:03:04.734 --> 00:03:06.834
Mona Lisa, Lisa Simpson?

00:03:06.834 --> 00:03:08.767
Even you have to admit
it's better than your real name,

00:03:08.767 --> 00:03:09.934
not Lisa.

00:03:09.934 --> 00:03:10.934
[ Laughter ]

00:03:10.934 --> 00:03:12.300
He says the word so many times,

00:03:12.300 --> 00:03:14.167
like he's in an episode
of "Seinfeld"

00:03:14.167 --> 00:03:15.667
where Kramer tells Jerry
about his plan

00:03:15.667 --> 00:03:18.334
to turn his entire apartment
into a series of hallways.

00:03:18.334 --> 00:03:20.033
[ As Kramer ]
One word, Jerry -- corridors.

00:03:20.033 --> 00:03:21.167
[ Laughter ]

00:03:21.167 --> 00:03:22.467
[ As Seinfeld ]
You got corridors here,

00:03:22.467 --> 00:03:24.400
corridors there,
it's all corridors.

00:03:24.400 --> 00:03:25.467
[ As George ]
They violated it, Jerry!

00:03:25.467 --> 00:03:26.934
They took away my corridor!

00:03:26.934 --> 00:03:28.467
[ As Elaine ]
Well, you'll never guess

00:03:28.467 --> 00:03:31.100
who took a trip
down my corridor.

00:03:31.100 --> 00:03:32.234
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:32.234 --> 00:03:33.667
[ As Seinfeld ]
Now, that's how you enter

00:03:33.667 --> 00:03:34.901
a corridor.

00:03:34.901 --> 00:03:36.534
[ "Seinfeld" theme sting ]

00:03:36.534 --> 00:03:39.634
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:03:39.634 --> 00:03:41.601
Keep a --

00:03:41.601 --> 00:03:43.734
Keep an eye out for my new
one-man show...

00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:46.667
[ Laughter ]

00:03:46.667 --> 00:03:48.300
When's it open?
It's closed?

00:03:48.300 --> 00:03:49.501
[ Laughter ]

00:03:49.501 --> 00:03:51.367
It hasn't even opened yet.
Can they do that?

00:03:51.367 --> 00:03:54.033
[ Laughter ]
Why didn't they call me?

00:03:54.033 --> 00:03:55.767
Oh, they thought I'd do
the voices on the phone?

00:03:55.767 --> 00:03:59.968
[ Laughter ]

00:03:59.968 --> 00:04:02.601
Anyway, despite Trump's drag
on the GOP in the midterms,

00:04:02.601 --> 00:04:03.767
it looks like
House Republicans

00:04:03.767 --> 00:04:05.167
have crawled
across the finish line

00:04:05.167 --> 00:04:06.767
and eked out a narrow majority
in the House,

00:04:06.767 --> 00:04:10.000
potentially making GOP leader
Kevin McCarthy the next speaker.

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:12.701
Now, McCarthy will have
a very small margin of error

00:04:12.701 --> 00:04:14.167
to work with,
given that Republicans

00:04:14.167 --> 00:04:16.167
will only have a few more votes
than Democrats.

00:04:16.167 --> 00:04:18.200
That probably means he won't be
able to get much done,

00:04:18.200 --> 00:04:20.300
although,
McCarthy dismissed the notion

00:04:20.300 --> 00:04:22.234
that the size of his majority
will matter.

00:04:22.234 --> 00:04:22.901
-What was our mission?

00:04:22.901 --> 00:04:24.400
To win the majority,

00:04:24.400 --> 00:04:25.868
to stop Biden's agenda,

00:04:25.868 --> 00:04:27.868
and fire Nancy Pelosi.

00:04:27.868 --> 00:04:29.501
All of that is accomplished.

00:04:29.501 --> 00:04:30.534
Remember, in the House,

00:04:30.534 --> 00:04:31.667
they don't give gavels out

00:04:31.667 --> 00:04:33.567
by small, medium, and large.

00:04:33.567 --> 00:04:35.067
They just give you the gavel.

00:04:35.067 --> 00:04:36.467
-Maybe they don't
give out gavels

00:04:36.467 --> 00:04:38.467
in small, medium, and large,
but they should.

00:04:38.467 --> 00:04:40.067
If you botch an election
that badly,

00:04:40.067 --> 00:04:41.801
but still manage
to eke out a narrow win,

00:04:41.801 --> 00:04:43.734
you should be forced
to call the House into section

00:04:43.734 --> 00:04:45.667
with a tiny, little gavel
the size of a pen.

00:04:45.667 --> 00:04:47.968
[ Laughter ]

00:04:47.968 --> 00:04:49.934
Also, don't give Donald Trump
any ideas.

00:04:49.934 --> 00:04:51.968
Because you know, as soon as he
heard McCarthy say that,

00:04:51.968 --> 00:04:54.234
Trump asked his team
to get him a giant gavel.

00:04:54.234 --> 00:04:56.033
[ Laughter ]
[ As Trump ]
I didn't even need to run

00:04:56.033 --> 00:04:57.434
because I've got
the biggest gavel

00:04:57.434 --> 00:04:59.334
and the guy who shows up
with the biggest gavel,

00:04:59.334 --> 00:05:00.801
he gets to be in charge.

00:05:00.801 --> 00:05:03.367
And you know what they say
about guys with gavels, right?

00:05:03.367 --> 00:05:04.968
Guys with big gavels.

00:05:04.968 --> 00:05:06.434
We all know they say,
don't they?

00:05:06.434 --> 00:05:08.567
They also have big carter-dors.

00:05:08.567 --> 00:05:12.334
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:12.334 --> 00:05:14.734
Plus,

00:05:14.734 --> 00:05:16.033
if Trump had a big gavel,

00:05:16.033 --> 00:05:17.934
he could play Whac-A-Mole
with his lawyers.

00:05:17.934 --> 00:05:20.200
[ As Giuliani ]
Boss, I got an idea!

00:05:20.200 --> 00:05:22.434
Ooh!
[ Whack ]

00:05:22.434 --> 00:05:24.100
You could've just said no, boss.

00:05:24.100 --> 00:05:25.501
[ Laughter ]

00:05:25.501 --> 00:05:26.934
Back in the hole.

00:05:26.934 --> 00:05:28.367
[ Laughter ]
Anyway,

00:05:28.367 --> 00:05:29.901
McCarthy's right
about one thing.

00:05:29.901 --> 00:05:32.234
He may not be able to pass much
of any legislation

00:05:32.234 --> 00:05:34.467
with such a slim majority,
but House Republicans

00:05:34.467 --> 00:05:36.534
will gain subpoena power,
along with the ability

00:05:36.534 --> 00:05:38.300
to run committees
and conduct investigations.

00:05:38.300 --> 00:05:40.300
In fact, they've already
announced their intentions

00:05:40.300 --> 00:05:42.100
to conduct nonsense
investigations

00:05:42.100 --> 00:05:44.133
into stuff like
Hunter Biden's laptop.

00:05:44.133 --> 00:05:46.234
Cartoon character lunatics,
like Marjorie Taylor Greene,

00:05:46.234 --> 00:05:48.634
might even have the power
to conduct oversight

00:05:48.634 --> 00:05:50.000
over the Biden administration,

00:05:50.000 --> 00:05:52.167
which Greene has repeatedly said
she would do aggressively.

00:05:52.167 --> 00:05:53.767
-I'm looking forward
to Republicans

00:05:53.767 --> 00:05:55.834
taking back control
in the House.

00:05:55.834 --> 00:05:59.767
[ Cheering, whistling,
and applause ]

00:05:59.767 --> 00:06:02.567
And I'm looking forward
to serving on committees.

00:06:02.567 --> 00:06:06.100
[ Cheering, whistling,
and applause ]

00:06:06.100 --> 00:06:09.534
Here's what you can expect
from Republicans.

00:06:09.534 --> 00:06:13.667
We will be investigating
and holding people accountable.

00:06:13.667 --> 00:06:15.634
There's a lot of traitors
and criminals

00:06:15.634 --> 00:06:17.467
that need to be
held accountable.

00:06:17.467 --> 00:06:18.734
-First of all,
I wouldn't trust anyone

00:06:18.734 --> 00:06:20.767
to conduct investigations
whose fashion style is

00:06:20.767 --> 00:06:22.400
Unabomber chic.
Also...

00:06:22.400 --> 00:06:24.400
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:24.400 --> 00:06:26.934
...this is why McCarthy's
majority is likely

00:06:26.934 --> 00:06:28.100
to be such a [bleep]show.

00:06:28.100 --> 00:06:29.767
He has the answer to crazies,
like Greene,

00:06:29.767 --> 00:06:32.667
who, in turn, answer to Trump,
in order to wield power

00:06:32.667 --> 00:06:35.000
because he has such
a slim majority.

00:06:35.000 --> 00:06:36.801
At any moment,
a few rogue Republicans

00:06:36.801 --> 00:06:38.067
could threaten
to take him down

00:06:38.067 --> 00:06:39.100
by withholding their votes,

00:06:39.100 --> 00:06:40.200
if they don't get
what they want.

00:06:40.200 --> 00:06:42.467
You can't function
in a job like that.

00:06:42.467 --> 00:06:43.868
Like, for example,
here at this job,

00:06:43.868 --> 00:06:45.400
I don't have to keep everyone
who works for me happy

00:06:45.400 --> 00:06:47.601
all the time, which is great,
because, if I did,

00:06:47.601 --> 00:06:49.334
I'd be constantly doling
out favors to everyone,

00:06:49.334 --> 00:06:51.167
like letting Wally
interrupt the show

00:06:51.167 --> 00:06:52.834
to plug his cue card business.

00:06:52.834 --> 00:06:55.234
-Seth, the holidays are right
around the corner,

00:06:55.234 --> 00:06:56.667
[ Laughter ]
so, if you're looking
for a unique gift

00:06:56.667 --> 00:06:58.267
for that special loved one
in your life,

00:06:58.267 --> 00:06:59.667
just go to cuecardsby--

00:06:59.667 --> 00:07:00.601
-Stop it!

00:07:00.601 --> 00:07:02.467
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:02.467 --> 00:07:03.334
See?

00:07:03.334 --> 00:07:05.801
I don't need to let him finish!

00:07:05.801 --> 00:07:07.234
Anyway, if you're looking
for a unique gift

00:07:07.234 --> 00:07:08.667
for that special loved one
in your life,

00:07:08.667 --> 00:07:10.267
just go to cuecardsbywally.com.

00:07:10.267 --> 00:07:11.467
Wait a second, damn it!

00:07:11.467 --> 00:07:13.334
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:13.334 --> 00:07:15.968
Did you write that on the cards
without my permission?!

00:07:15.968 --> 00:07:16.901
-Did I?

00:07:16.901 --> 00:07:18.167
Oops!

00:07:18.167 --> 00:07:21.067
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:21.067 --> 00:07:24.567
[ Cheering ]

00:07:24.567 --> 00:07:26.000
You're my
Marjorie Taylor Greene.

00:07:26.000 --> 00:07:28.934
[ Laughter ]

00:07:34.334 --> 00:07:37.601
Can we edit out the long,
trailing giggle of...

00:07:37.601 --> 00:07:41.100
[ Laughter ]

00:07:41.100 --> 00:07:43.234
We call that sound effect
Wally's Delight.

00:07:43.234 --> 00:07:44.868
[ Laughter ]

00:07:44.868 --> 00:07:46.634
Anyway,
these are the kinds of bozos

00:07:46.634 --> 00:07:48.367
Trump surrounds himself with
and, now, they will have

00:07:48.367 --> 00:07:50.300
a very tenuous hold
on power in the House,

00:07:50.300 --> 00:07:51.534
which is bad for everyone,

00:07:51.534 --> 00:07:52.968
including Republicans,
themselves,

00:07:52.968 --> 00:07:55.567
because Trump's handpicked slate
of election denier candidates

00:07:55.567 --> 00:07:57.300
performed horribly
in last week's midterms,

00:07:57.300 --> 00:07:59.934
especially compared to other,
more traditional Republicans.

00:07:59.934 --> 00:08:02.901
Voters thoroughly rejected
Trumpism and the MAGA movement

00:08:02.901 --> 00:08:04.834
and made clear they want
a competent government

00:08:04.834 --> 00:08:06.334
that will preserve
American democracy.

00:08:06.334 --> 00:08:08.968
That's why Republicans
are also nervous about Georgia,

00:08:08.968 --> 00:08:10.968
where Trump-backed Senate
candidate Herschel Walker

00:08:10.968 --> 00:08:13.400
finished second
and will head to a runoff

00:08:13.400 --> 00:08:15.000
against incumbent
Raphael Warnock.

00:08:15.000 --> 00:08:16.868
And Walker
is not helping himself,

00:08:16.868 --> 00:08:18.734
as evidenced
by this incredibly bizarre

00:08:18.734 --> 00:08:21.000
and completely real clip
from a rally yesterday

00:08:21.000 --> 00:08:23.467
where Walker told
an inscrutable story

00:08:23.467 --> 00:08:24.534
about watching a movie

00:08:24.534 --> 00:08:26.300
about vampires
and werewolves on TV.

00:08:26.300 --> 00:08:27.701
See if you can follow --

00:08:27.701 --> 00:08:29.267
best of luck to you --
any of this.

00:08:29.267 --> 00:08:30.467
[ Laughter ]
-You ever watch a stupid movie

00:08:30.467 --> 00:08:31.934
late at night,
hoping it's going to get better,

00:08:31.934 --> 00:08:33.601
it don't get better, but you
keep watching it, anyway?

00:08:33.601 --> 00:08:35.200
[ Laughter ]
Because, the other night,

00:08:35.200 --> 00:08:36.901
the other night,
I was watching this movie.

00:08:36.901 --> 00:08:38.767
I was watching this movie called
"Fright Night,"

00:08:38.767 --> 00:08:40.467
Freak Night --
some type of night.

00:08:40.467 --> 00:08:42.534
But it was about vampires.
I don't know if you know,

00:08:42.534 --> 00:08:44.567
vampires are some cool people,
are they not?

00:08:44.567 --> 00:08:46.567
[ Laughter ]
But I'mma tell you something
that I found out.

00:08:46.567 --> 00:08:49.067
A werewolf can kill a vampire.
Did you know that?

00:08:49.067 --> 00:08:51.133
[ Laughter ]
I never knew that, so I don't
want to be a vampire anymore.

00:08:51.133 --> 00:08:52.434
I want to be a werewolf.

00:08:52.434 --> 00:08:54.801
But then, anyway,
as I'm watching this movie --

00:08:54.801 --> 00:08:56.100
And let me tell you
how stupid it is

00:08:56.100 --> 00:08:57.267
because it's 1:00
in the morning.

00:08:57.267 --> 00:08:59.234
So, I'm watching my TV

00:08:59.234 --> 00:09:01.400
of these kids watching their TV,

00:09:01.400 --> 00:09:04.033
of a vampire killer
on their TV.

00:09:04.033 --> 00:09:05.100
So, you know
it's kind of stupid,

00:09:05.100 --> 00:09:06.033
but I'm still watching it,
though.

00:09:06.033 --> 00:09:07.634
As I'm watching this show,

00:09:07.634 --> 00:09:09.467
what was funny,
these kids had a vampire

00:09:09.467 --> 00:09:12.033
in their attic at their house.

00:09:12.033 --> 00:09:14.501
So they was watching their TV.

00:09:14.501 --> 00:09:16.367
Now I watch my TV,
they're watching their TV,

00:09:16.367 --> 00:09:18.667
they see the vampire killer
on their TV.

00:09:18.667 --> 00:09:20.834
So, they win this contest
to bring this actor --

00:09:20.834 --> 00:09:22.267
Now, y'all got
to stay with me.

00:09:22.267 --> 00:09:23.767
-Oh, it's way...

00:09:23.767 --> 00:09:25.434
[ Laughter ]

00:09:25.434 --> 00:09:27.601
...way too late
to stay with you, friend.

00:09:27.601 --> 00:09:28.868
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:09:28.868 --> 00:09:32.334
That was, by far, the worst
Rotten Tomatoes synopsis

00:09:32.334 --> 00:09:33.200
I've ever heard.

00:09:33.200 --> 00:09:35.567
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:09:35.567 --> 00:09:36.801
You sound like an eight-year-old

00:09:36.801 --> 00:09:38.400
who ate too much sugar
on Halloween

00:09:38.400 --> 00:09:40.667
and stayed up watching TV
way past his bedtime.

00:09:40.667 --> 00:09:42.467
"Did you know that werewolves
can kill vampires?

00:09:42.467 --> 00:09:43.901
I didn't know that,
so, I don't want to be

00:09:43.901 --> 00:09:45.367
a vampire anymore,
I want to be a werewolf.

00:09:45.367 --> 00:09:47.467
And also, did you know that the
human head weighs eight pounds?"

00:09:47.467 --> 00:09:49.000
[ Laughter ]

00:09:49.000 --> 00:09:51.167
All I got in that story
was the sentence --

00:09:51.167 --> 00:09:53.067
and let me make sure
I'm reading this verbatim,

00:09:53.067 --> 00:09:56.033
so I can be fair and accurate
to the potential future

00:09:56.033 --> 00:09:57.601
United States Senator
from Georgia --

00:09:57.601 --> 00:09:58.534
[ Laughter ]

00:09:58.534 --> 00:09:59.934
[ Clears throat ]

00:09:59.934 --> 00:10:01.567
"I don't know if you know,

00:10:01.567 --> 00:10:03.767
vampires are cool people,
are they not?"

00:10:03.767 --> 00:10:06.334
[ Laughter ]

00:10:06.334 --> 00:10:08.634
Can you imagine someone
actually asking that question

00:10:08.634 --> 00:10:10.701
during a hearing
in the Senate chamber?

00:10:10.701 --> 00:10:12.868
[ Southern accent ]
The chair recognizes
the senator from Georgia,

00:10:12.868 --> 00:10:13.968
while also reminding him

00:10:13.968 --> 00:10:15.701
that this hearing is
about agriculture

00:10:15.701 --> 00:10:17.634
and that our witness is
an expert on grain,

00:10:17.634 --> 00:10:19.567
not vampires."

00:10:19.567 --> 00:10:21.167
[ As Walker ]
Okay, cool. [ Clears throat ]

00:10:21.167 --> 00:10:23.167
Mr. Secretary, before I get
to the issue of farm subsidies,

00:10:23.167 --> 00:10:24.234
I have one question for you --

00:10:24.234 --> 00:10:25.734
vampires are cool people,
are they not?

00:10:25.734 --> 00:10:29.367
[ Laughter ]

00:10:29.367 --> 00:10:30.901
I yield the rest of my time.

00:10:30.901 --> 00:10:32.634
[ Laughter ]

00:10:32.634 --> 00:10:35.767
Also, let me just say,
I did know that, okay?

00:10:35.767 --> 00:10:38.801
[ Laughter ]
Let's be honest,
vampires are kickass people.

00:10:38.801 --> 00:10:41.234
There's no debate about that.

00:10:41.234 --> 00:10:43.634
Some of my best friends
are vampires.

00:10:43.634 --> 00:10:45.000
[ Laughter ]

00:10:45.000 --> 00:10:46.601
Why do you think
I look older every year,

00:10:46.601 --> 00:10:48.501
but Colin Jost
still looks like this?

00:10:48.501 --> 00:10:50.334
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:10:50.334 --> 00:10:53.033
He is 238 years old.

00:10:53.033 --> 00:10:54.067
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:10:54.067 --> 00:10:55.200
Not only did he just buy

00:10:55.200 --> 00:10:57.167
an old Staten Island ferry,

00:10:57.167 --> 00:10:58.834
he was on the inaugural journey.

00:10:58.834 --> 00:11:01.400
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:11:03.367 --> 00:11:04.300
Now, you've heard it all.

00:11:04.300 --> 00:11:05.634
If you were at all worried

00:11:05.634 --> 00:11:07.534
that the story just abruptly
ended there

00:11:07.534 --> 00:11:08.701
and Walker moved on
to something

00:11:08.701 --> 00:11:09.934
that made more sense, you know,

00:11:09.934 --> 00:11:12.601
to the voters of Georgia...

00:11:12.601 --> 00:11:13.667
[ Laughter ]

00:11:13.667 --> 00:11:14.901
...rest assured,
he kept going

00:11:14.901 --> 00:11:16.968
and the rest of it
was just as bizarre.

00:11:16.968 --> 00:11:18.667
In fact,
the story about vampires,

00:11:18.667 --> 00:11:20.167
or whatever, was so long,

00:11:20.167 --> 00:11:24.267
the only way for us to show it
to you is through a time lapse.

00:11:24.267 --> 00:11:26.868
-Bring this actor who's
a vampire killer from that TV

00:11:26.868 --> 00:11:29.200
to get rid of this real-life
vampire in their attic.

00:11:29.200 --> 00:11:31.067
Got to have a stake
and got to have a thing

00:11:31.067 --> 00:11:32.367
that kill him in the heart.

00:11:32.367 --> 00:11:34.801
And he got a necklace
of garlic because that work.

00:11:34.801 --> 00:11:36.167
I don't know what it does,
but it work.

00:11:36.167 --> 00:11:37.667
Got to have a cross
because it burns.

00:11:37.667 --> 00:11:38.667
I know that works.

00:11:38.667 --> 00:11:40.300
They walked upstairs
and this vampire

00:11:40.300 --> 00:11:42.100
looking real good
in this black suit.

00:11:42.100 --> 00:11:44.667
He floated from the ceiling,
looking good and cool.

00:11:44.667 --> 00:11:45.734
And I'm thinking, "Whoa!

00:11:45.734 --> 00:11:46.834
They better get
out of that house."

00:11:46.834 --> 00:11:48.234
They jumped behind the hero.

00:11:48.234 --> 00:11:49.934
They guy jumped in front of him
with this holy water,

00:11:49.934 --> 00:11:51.067
threw it
on the vampire forehead.

00:11:51.067 --> 00:11:52.000
He covered his eyes.

00:11:52.000 --> 00:11:52.968
He took the cross.

00:11:52.968 --> 00:11:54.601
He put it
on the vampire forehead

00:11:54.601 --> 00:11:56.100
and the vampire
didn't even do anything.

00:11:56.100 --> 00:11:57.567
He said, "That don't work."

00:11:57.567 --> 00:11:58.634
And that's the way it is
in our life.

00:11:58.634 --> 00:11:59.667
It doesn't even work.

00:11:59.667 --> 00:12:01.400
-I think Herschel Walker's plan

00:12:01.400 --> 00:12:02.601
to combat inflation

00:12:02.601 --> 00:12:04.400
might be that no one in Georgia
will need to pay

00:12:04.400 --> 00:12:05.701
for streaming services anymore

00:12:05.701 --> 00:12:07.467
[ Laughter ]
because he'll just tell you

00:12:07.467 --> 00:12:10.000
the plots of movies
and TV shows.

00:12:10.000 --> 00:12:11.968
[ As Walker ]
Now, there are no actual squids
in "Squid Game,"

00:12:11.968 --> 00:12:13.234
but that doesn't mean
these people don't have

00:12:13.234 --> 00:12:14.467
some serious problems.

00:12:14.467 --> 00:12:15.467
[ Laughter ]

00:12:15.467 --> 00:12:16.467
Trump and his movement

00:12:16.467 --> 00:12:18.167
were clearly
a major drag on the GOP.

00:12:18.167 --> 00:12:20.167
in last week's midterms,
which gave Republicans

00:12:20.167 --> 00:12:22.100
an incredibly narrow majority
in the House

00:12:22.100 --> 00:12:24.434
that will probably be led,
in large part,

00:12:24.434 --> 00:12:27.033
by fringe extremists looking
to cause chaos, and who knows?

00:12:27.033 --> 00:12:29.267
In a few weeks, they might even
be joined by Herschel Walker,

00:12:29.267 --> 00:12:31.501
who, if he gets to the Senate,

00:12:31.501 --> 00:12:34.467
will be walking around looking
for werewolves and vampires

00:12:34.467 --> 00:12:35.300
hiding in all the...

00:12:35.300 --> 00:12:36.133
-Carters.

00:12:36.133 --> 00:12:39.767
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:12:39.767 --> 00:12:42.267
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:12:42.267 --> 00:12:45.968
♪♪
[ Cheering and applause ]

